From a490cda99ea469b5509294b4e8dc04b53b75738a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:44:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] Move: the rules outside battle go from game-state.js to
 game/js/logic/rules.js

65 names, same code (node tools/move-names.mjs verify: 64 statements moved, nothing else changed): the helpers
cleanName, formatNumber, stepsToKm, newUid, today, plural, pickWeighted; a Billie's numbers (xpFor, maxLevel,
moveSlotCount, teamSize, stat, maxHp, movesAt, makeBilly...), evolution, team and storage; steps and their money
(STEP_BRACKETS...); the trip along the roads and its gates; encounters (encounterPoolHere, spawn); addSteps; eggs;
day jobs. game-state.js keeps the state and where it is stored (saveData, activeBattle, uiState, reducedMotion,
localStorage, save, flushSave), escapeHtml and, until the next commit, the save format.

rules.js comes right after game-data.js on the game's page. What it reads from game-state.js and the interface
(saveData, uiState, activeBattle, save, toast, render, jingle...) now comes through hooks.js, filled as before. Only
STEP_BRACKETS (and the statement that closes its last bracket) is worked out at load, now a little earlier, from
RULES alone. The modules that used these names import them from rules.js (tools/to-module.mjs).

Checked: lint (rules.js passes with no browser globals), check:modules, format, build, smoke 14/14 (161 s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LpFSn4GaodAVzjKW5J3oQR
